Package: multiScaleAC
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Scale Spatial Autocorrelation with Moran's I
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-09-08
Authors@R:
    c(
      person("Alex", "Soupir", , "alex.soupir@moffitt.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Computes bivariate Moran's I as a function of Gaussian kernel
    bandwidth, yielding a functional curve over spatial scales rather than a
    single value at one arbitrarily chosen scale. Weights are taken directly
    from the kernel with row standardisation and no minimum weight threshold,
    so no spots or cells are discarded from the weight matrix. Intended for
    ligand-receptor interaction analysis in spatial transcriptomics, and
    interoperable with functional data analysis via 'mxfda'. Implements the
    method described in Soupir et al. (2026) <doi:10.64898/2026.07.14.738306>.
